raw:
I have enough from the renders to diagnose directly. The build's walls read well (cobblestone panels framed by stone-brick piers/quoins/plinth — matches the concept), but the entire top is an open, roofless shell: the dark planks lie flat as sagging interior beams instead of forming the steep enclosing gable.

```json
{
  "items": [
    {
      "department": "ROOF",
      "expected": "a tall steep gable roof clad across its whole field in dark_oak_planks, ridge running along the long (x) axis, fully enclosing the mass with overhanging eaves",
      "present": "a few dark planks lying flat and sagging across the open top as loose beams/lean-tos; the mass is left open to the sky",
      "missing": "the pitched gable covering itself — no continuous sloped plank field, no ridge, no enclosure",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "department": "WALL",
      "expected": "the gable-end triangle above the eave continues in the same cobblestone fieldstone, closing each short wall up to the ridge",
      "present": "the short walls stop at eave height; the triangular gable infill is open",
      "missing": "the cobblestone gable-end triangle above the eave on both ends",
      "severity": "major"
    },
    {
      "department": "OPENING",
      "expected": "two oak_planks wagon doors on the long +z eave wall, kept bright and distinct from the dark roof",
      "present": "openings in the bays but no distinct oak wagon-door leaves are read",
      "missing": "the two golden oak wagon doors",
      "severity": "minor"
    }
  ]
}
```
